D1: PostgreSQL databases on Membership hosts
timeseries up = avg(postgres.uptime, scalar: true), by:{device.name, device}, from:-2h
| fieldsAdd hostShort = lower(splitString(device.name, ".")[0])
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.host
    | fields hostName = entity.name, tags
    | expand t = tags
    | filter startsWith(t, "APMID:")
    | fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(t, "APMID:")[1],
                hostShort = lower(splitString(hostName, ".")[0])
    | filter in(apmid, array($MembershipApps))
    | summarize apps = collectDistinct(apmid), by:{hostShort}
  ], sourceField: hostShort, lookupField: hostShort, prefix: "h."
| filter isNotNull(h.apps)
| expand apmid = h.apps
| summarize databases = countDistinctExact(device),
            servers   = countDistinctExact(device.name),
            by:{apmid}
| sort databases desc

D2: MSSQL databases on Membership hosts
timeseries st = max(`sql-server.databases.state`, scalar: true),
           by:{device.name, database}, from:-30m
| fieldsAdd hostShort = lower(splitString(device.name, ".")[0])
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.host
    | fields hostName = entity.name, tags
    | expand t = tags
    | filter startsWith(t, "APMID:")
    | fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(t, "APMID:")[1],
                hostShort = lower(splitString(hostName, ".")[0])
    | filter in(apmid, array($MembershipApps))
    | summarize apps = collectDistinct(apmid), by:{hostShort}
  ], sourceField: hostShort, lookupField: hostShort, prefix: "h."
| filter isNotNull(h.apps)
| expand apmid = h.apps
| summarize databases = countDistinctExact(concat(device.name, "|", database)),
            servers   = countDistinctExact(device.name),
            notOnline = countIf(st > 0),
            by:{apmid}
| sort databases desc


For both, send the number of apps and the top rows. If a query returns nothing, Membership has no database of that type on its hosts, and that tile is dropped.

D3: Other database technologies on Membership processes

This catches databases we haven't looked at, such as Oracle or DB2.

fetch dt.entity.process_group_instance
| fields id, softwareTechnologies, tags
| expand tag = tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($MembershipApps))
| expand tech = softwareTechnologies
| fieldsAdd t = lower(toString(tech))
| filter contains(t, "db2") or contains(t, "sql") or contains(t, "oracle") or contains(t, "mongo") or contains(t, "postgre")
| summarize instances = countDistinctExact(id), apps = countDistinctExact(apmid), by:{t}
| sort apps desc


Ignore sqlite and the Java vendor entries mentioning Oracle, as with Claims.

D4: MQ alerts that name a Membership app
fetch dt.davis.problems, from:-90d
| sort timestamp desc
| dedup display_id
| filter contains(event.name, "IBMMQ_APP")
| fieldsAdd apmid = concat("APP", substring(splitString(event.name, "IBMMQ_APP")[1], from:0, to:8))
| filter in(apmid, array($MembershipApps))
| summarize alerts = count(), active = countIf(event.status == "ACTIVE"), by:{apmid}
| sort alerts desc


No rows means either Membership doesn't use MQ or its alerts follow a different naming pattern. I can't tell which from this query, so D5 checks the second case.

D5: Which problem types hit Membership apps
fetch dt.davis.problems, from:-30d
| sort timestamp desc
| dedup display_id
| filter dt.davis.is_duplicate == false
| expand tag = entity_tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($MembershipApps))
| dedup display_id
| summarize problems = count(),
            active   = countIf(event.status == "ACTIVE"),
            apps     = countDistinctExact(apmid),
            by:{event.name}
| sort problems desc
| limit 25
